## 🟡 Remaining / Reduced

### F2: Utility Duplication — 4 Local Wrappers Remain

All 4 delegate to `shared/scalars.ts` — they are thin adapters, not inline copies:

| File | Function | Delegates to |
|---|---|---|
| `globalSettingsAdmin.ts:211` | `clampInt(value, min, max, fallback)` | `clampIntOr(value, fallback, min, max)` |
| `adminScout/support.ts:103` | `clampInt(value, fallback, min, max)` | `clampIntOr(value, fallback, min, max)` |
| `adminActivity.ts:38` | `clampInt(v, lo, hi, fallback)` | `clampIntOr(v, fallback, lo, hi)` |
| `griftRetention.ts:38` | `clampInt(value, min, max, fallback)` | `clampIntOr(value, fallback, min, max, "round")` |

> [!NOTE]
> Per `.agents/audit-decomposition.md`: *"local wrappers are allowed when semantics differ"*. These preserve legacy call-site arg order. `griftRetention` also sets rounding mode `"round"`. Risk of silent wrong clamping (the P0 concern) is eliminated because the wrappers call the canonical implementation.

**Verdict:** No-action. The latent bug risk cited in the report is resolved.

